  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - Provision A.4(7) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) requires that where any owner/occupier of any adjoin premises objects to a proposed development, the local planning authority must assess the impacts of the proposed development on the amenity impacts on neighbouring properties.\r\nObjections have been received and as such, the application was assessed against the Local Planning Authority's policies in regard to neighbour amenity. \r\nThe development would by reason of its scale and design, result in an increased sense of enclosure, loss of outlook, and overbearing impact for adjoining residents at No.2 Rowditch Road. Furthermore, the application has failed to demonstrate that it would not result in harmful loss of daylight to the neighbouring window. The proposal therefore fails to comply with policy LP2 of the Wandsworth Local Plan 2023 and Wandsworth Housing SPD (2016).\r\n\r\n"
  ],
